<title>UK: V-Ships declines to comment on Cunard report.</title>
<headline>V-Ships declines to comment on Cunard report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>V-Ships, the Monaco-based ship management firm, on Tuesday declined to comment on a report that it would like to manage Cunard's cruise ship fleet if the vessels are sold by Norway's Kvaerner ASA.</p>
<p>Roberto Giorgi, V-Ships' managing director, said: &quot;I am afraid I have no comment to make on the matter.&quot;</p>
<p>Shipping newspaper Lloyd's List reported on Tuesday that Cunard was one of a number of projects under consideration by V-Ships, although the company has ruled out acquisition of Cunard itself.</p>
<p>&quot;We probably have 25-30 projects on the go at any one time. Cunard is one of them,&quot; Giorgi told the paper. But he added: &quot;We are not now in the business of owning ships.&quot;</p>
<p>--Reuters Shipping Desk +44 171 542 4087/4012 Fax 542 5017</p>
